From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Masakazu Kitajo <maskit@apache.org>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 16:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Resolve OpenSSL 4.0 build issues

OpenSSL 4.0 makes ASN1_STRING opaque, and X509_get_subject_name(),
X509_NAME_get_entry(), X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_data() and
X509_REQ_get_subject_name() now return const pointers.

Backport of upstream commit bdefaf97b6 (released in 10.2.0) to 9.2.15.
Differences from the upstream commit:

- Paths: iocore/net/ and src/traffic_server/InkAPI.cc instead of
  src/iocore/net/ and src/api/InkAPI.cc.
- Explicit const types where upstream uses auto. Upstream uses auto to
  keep building against OpenSSL 1.1.1.
- plugins/certifier: mkcsr() exists only in 9.2.x. It added the CN to
  the name that X509_REQ_get_subject_name() returns, which is const in
  OpenSSL 4. It now builds the name with X509_NAME_new() and sets it
  with X509_REQ_set_subject_name(). mkcrt() keeps the CSR subject const.
  This mkcsr() hunk is Chainguard-written, not upstream code. Upstream's
  matching fix is in mkcrt() and uses X509_NAME_dup() with a
  scoped_X509_NAME.
- Smaller differences: the InkAPI.cc hunk does not carry upstream's
  "const int pos", and the changed lines were not re-run through
  clang-format.
- Left out: hunks for code that 9.2.15 does not have (cripts, txn_box,
  the lua certificate helpers, the OCSP certificate-ID functions,
  test_SSLDHParams) or does not build by default (experimental and
  example plugins).

Upstream: https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/pull/13476
Co-authored-by: Jered Floyd <jered@redhat.com>
